WHATNOW

What tamlinux is doing now and what comes next. Read this first; revise
it at the end of every session (work/README-work).

Updated: 2026-11-21, with W7


STATE

  Version 0.0.4 on branch dev (uncommitted working tree, ready for Fred's
  trial). Scrollback and pointer support are implemented and verified:
  - Scrollback in 64-row pages capped at 4096 rows (primary screen),
    navigated with wheel and Shift+PgUp/PgDn; ED 3 clears scrollback.
  - wl_pointer and optional wp_cursor_shape_v1 (text I-beam in normal
    mode, default arrow in mouse reporting mode).
  - Text selection (drag, double-click word, triple-click line) with
    inverted cell rendering and UTF-8 extraction.
  - Clipboard (wl_data_device) and optional primary selection
    (zwp_primary_selection_v1): Ctrl+Shift+C/V, Shift+Insert, middle
    click, and bracketed paste (DECSET 2004).
  - Mouse reporting (1000, 1002, 1003, SGR 1006) with Shift bypass.

  make test (test_wire 114, test_vt 297, test_ttf 3036, test_keys 78,
  test_render 25, version 0.0.4, headless tam-pane), ASan/UBSan sanitize
  tests, and readelf -d (libc and libm only) all pass.


